Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 item shop plates hang from the 16:9 edges

The item shop (STITSHOP) already had the scrolling backdrop in the gutters
(patch 0053), but its plates were still at the 4:3 positions: the money bar,
the BUY / SELL panel, the Back hint and the buy and sell dialogs hang from
the right edge (a 4:3 picture cuts them off at x 320), and the bars of the
details panel and the item list run off both edges, so in 16:9 their ends
showed in the gutters. Drawing only; gated on the gutter (off, every
position is the PS1 one). Same helpers as patches 0076 and 0101-0104:

- shop.c: the money bar, the BUY / SELL panel and the Back hint move to the
  16:9 right edge (DW3_MENU_RIGHT) with the money, BUY, SELL and help windows,
  the cursor and the open-animation pivots. The shop's name plate is inside
  the picture and stays.
- item_list.c: the list frame is widened (DW3_MENU_BAND); the L1 / R1 hints
  and their page arrows go to its ends (DW3_MENU_LEFT / DW3_MENU_RIGHT).
- info.c: the details panel's name bar is widened at its joint (BAND, split
  136) so its item name and icon hang from the left edge and the equip,
  owned and price cells (windows too) from the right edge; the description
  box is widened (BAND); the "Button: Effects" plate hangs from the left
  edge. The partner stats page (three panels) stays in the middle.
- trade.c: the buy and sell dialogs (How many?, the total with its Yes / No,
  Equip?, the sell kinds) hang from the right edge with their windows,
  cursors and pivots.

Test hook (PC only, like DW3_FORCE_ITEMS of patch 0070): DW3_FORCE_MONEY=<bit>
sets the money when the shop opens, and the shop honours DW3_FORCE_ITEMS
too, so a replay reaches the buy and sell screens without playing for
money and drops. Logs "dw3: DW3_FORCE_MONEY money N". Unset (every release,
and the Switch) it does nothing.

